    {
        "content": "<p>Huh, this looks like a bug and will investigate. Indeed, <code>vcgen</code> is currently on prototype status, but these experiments are exactly what is needed to lift that :)</p>\n<p>If you are looking for inspiration, here are more examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/master/tests/bench/vcgen/vcgen_imp.lean\">https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/master/tests/bench/vcgen/vcgen_imp.lean</a> (which I need to relocate) is an exploration of pretty much the same use case as yours. I start from an omnisemantics, which takes the place of your set of axioms. Relying on axioms seems a bit ugly. Firstly, they are axioms, but secondly you can't eliminate a <code>wp</code> proof without further axioms. The omnisemantics allows equivalence proofs to other semantic encodings without any axioms whatsoever. If I were going for an axiomatic semantics, I think I'd encode the Hoare logic using an inductive Prop.</li>\n<li>Here's a (very bare bones) separation logic prototype: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/master/tests/elab/vcgenSepLogic.lean\">https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/master/tests/elab/vcgenSepLogic.lean</a></li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 612112617,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Graf",
        "timestamp": 1784720387
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Cool, thanks for the links!  By the way, I'm just using axioms because this is also a small experiment to learn how <code>vcgen</code> works, and in my real project I will be using a similar omnisemantics. In fact I think the axioms as stated are actually \"wrong\", though fortunately that does not matter here.</p>",
        "id": 612114059,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1784720872
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A few bugs that I need to fix:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Without <code>open Lean.Order</code>, the convenient post notation <code>⦃ Φ ⦄</code> instead of <code>⦃ Φ; epost⟨⟩⦄</code> does not work because \\bottom cannot be resolved. Hmm.</li>\n<li>An arrow on the RHS of ⊑ brings VC generation to a halt; that's what is causing <code>vcgen</code> to \"exit early\".</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 612114171,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Graf",
        "timestamp": 1784720920
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Fixed in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/14497\">lean4#14497</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/14502\">lean4#14502</a>.</p>",
        "id": 612152713,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Graf",
        "timestamp": 1784731463
    }
]